# No em dashes in user-facing copy

In text that users see (What's New, i18n JSON, marketing/FAQ, store listings, in-app toasts and screens), **do not use the em dash `—`** (U+2014) or en dash `–` (U+2013).

Use a normal hyphen-minus **`-`** instead.

```text
❌ bez Premium — przeglądasz
✅ bez Premium - przeglądasz
```

Internal/tech docs (e.g. `docs/releases/*.md`, code comments) may keep other punctuation if already established; prefer `-` when writing new user-facing strings.
